  "body": "Steps 5-7 of https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#fetch-finale don't work for opaque responses. We want to actually give a signal after the entire body is read which if we're just looking at the filtered response wouldn't work because body would be null. And despite it being somewhat unsafe, I think @domenic also expressed that he would expect callers of \"process response consume body\" to get all the bytes of an opaque response without ceremony.\r\n\r\nFound as part of #1509. Should maybe be fixed together with #1511.\r\n\r\ncc @noamr ",
